#!/bin/sh
# Starts the graphical NoCapOS installer (Calamares with NoCapOS's settings
# and look, /etc/calamares) from the live session, the way Debian's own
# launcher does: as root through polkit, on this session's screen.
set -u
if pgrep -x calamares >/dev/null 2>&1; then exit 0; fi
export QT_AUTO_SCREEN_SCALE_FACTOR=1
# The live user may use sudo without a password: no password helper is
# needed then (NoCap Desktop runs none, so pkexec would fail silently).
if sudo -n true 2>/dev/null; then
  exec sudo -n env WAYLAND_DISPLAY="${WAYLAND_DISPLAY:-}" XDG_RUNTIME_DIR="${XDG_RUNTIME_DIR:-}"     DISPLAY="${DISPLAY:-}" QT_QPA_PLATFORM="wayland;xcb" QT_AUTO_SCREEN_SCALE_FACTOR=1 calamares
fi
if [ -x /usr/bin/calamares-install-debian ]; then
  exec /usr/bin/calamares-install-debian
fi
xhost +si:localuser:root >/dev/null 2>&1 || true
pkexec calamares
rc=$?
xhost -si:localuser:root >/dev/null 2>&1 || true
exit "$rc"
